. El contrato [1], de 14.479,82 euros, se adjudicó en octubre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no implica irregularidades. Puede deberse a razones legítimas, como necesidades específicas o precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en años distintos. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen por necesidades específicas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 31 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 3.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 8.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.7 to 16.4. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 24% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,479.82 euros, was awarded in October 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices may be low, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical patterns don't indicate improper actions.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts cover the same need. Review awardee A's contracts for patterns. Look at contract [1] for its date and amount to see if it fits a trend.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["EhhZZpSe8wtVYjgxA4nMUw%3D%3D","ZwAQJH9XtX4%2Bk2oCbDosIw%3D%3D","Klb8jiMy5WV4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}